  $q$```csharp
int x = 10;
if (x >= 29)
    if (x <= 0)
        Console.Write("A");
else
    Console.Write("B");
```
Čo vypíše tento kód?$q$,
  array[$q$`A`$q$, $q$Nič$q$, $q$`B`$q$, $q$`AB`$q$], 1, $q$`else` patrí k najbližšiemu `if` – teda k `if (x <= 0)`, aj keď je odsadený inak. `x >= 29` je `false`, takže sa celý vnútorný `if` aj s `else` preskočí.$q$,
  $q$```csharp
int x = 10;
if (x >= 29)
    if (x <= 0)
        Console.Write("A");
else
    Console.Write("B");
```
What does this code print?$q$,
  array[$q$`A`$q$, $q$Nothing$q$, $q$`B`$q$, $q$`AB`$q$], $q$`else` belongs to the nearest `if` – `if (x <= 0)` – even though it's indented differently. `x >= 29` is `false`, so the whole inner `if` including the `else` is skipped.$q$);

